// What ohpm resolves for this module, and the one dependency it has.
//
// `marsrs-harmonyos-xlog` is the HAR of the port: the ArkTS `Xlog` over the NAPI
// module, with `libmarsrs_xlog.so` and the Rust core inside it.
//
// It is taken from `libs/` and not from ohpm's central repository, because
// publishing to ohpm is not switched on yet — the HarmonyOS section of
// `docs/xlog/getting-started.md` says so, and `scripts/package_harmony.sh`
// writes the same archive a release carries. So the HAR is downloaded once, out
// of the release, and `file:` is what points ohpm at a package on disk:
//
//   gh release download v0.1.0-alpha.3 --pattern 'marsrs-harmonyos-xlog-*.har' \
//       --dir demo/harmonyos/libs
//   mv demo/harmonyos/libs/marsrs-harmonyos-xlog-*.har \
//       demo/harmonyos/libs/marsrs-harmonyos-xlog.har
//   ohpm install
//
// The rename is the point of the second line: a release asset carries the
// version of the release — the download above is a
// `marsrs-harmonyos-xlog-0.1.0-alpha.3.har` today — and a `file:` dependency
// that named one version is a dependency that names no file at all after the
// next release. `libs/` is one HAR that is whatever version was downloaded, so
// the name here has no version in it.
//
// The line an app writes once the package *is* on ohpm is
// `"marsrs-harmonyos-xlog": "^1.0.0"`, and nothing else in the module changes.
{
  "name": "entry",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "The HarmonyOS demo of mars-rs: one button that writes six records into a .xlog file.",
  "main": "",
  "author": "orangeboyChen",
  "license": "MIT",
  "dependencies": {
    "marsrs-harmonyos-xlog": "file:../libs/marsrs-harmonyos-xlog.har"
  }
}
